WEBVTT

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.510
Man, where did that cat go?

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:06.730
She didn't even touch her food.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.220
Hey, Fug!

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:10.230
Fug!

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.590
I'm leaving!

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:24.920
I'm had enough of this place!

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:26.290
Calm down, man!

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:48.520
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:09.810
<b>Shrine and Temple</b>

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.620
Jeez...

00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:19.160
Is this gonna be a dry summer?

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:21.620
There are a lot of trees around.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:23.960
This is a temple, Haru.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:25.090
A temple?

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:29.690
Man, this is all because you said 
you wanted to meet the lion-dogs.

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:31.380
What a pain...

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:34.800
I'm very sorry, Gintaro-sama.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:36.600
It's okay.

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.050
We wanted to show you around town.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:42.030
If you're not happy, go back to sleep.

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:44.220
I would if I could.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:45.960
What's taking you so long?

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:47.400
Just come over!

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:48.880
Yeah, I get it.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:50.390
Just hurry up.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:50.390
That voice sounds familiar...

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:53.350
Come on...

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:55.900
Oh, it's Mako-chan.

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:58.610
Shohei-kun, why are you here?

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:06.080
<b>Amabuki Temple</b>

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:00.900
This is my home.

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:03.040
Really?

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.710
This is a big temple.

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:06.500
Nah, it's old as dirt.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:08.260
Was that Yumi-chan?

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:09.700
Bingo.

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:12.080
She wants to come see Fug.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:13.040
You're really close.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:15.560
What about you, Mako-chan?

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:16.290
Is that your boyfriend?

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.110
N-No!

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:20.720
He's a friend of the family 
from another shrine.

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:23.910
Why are you blushing?!

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:25.220
I'm not!

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:26.400
Huh?

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.080
N-Nothing!

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:29.390
<i>R-Right...</i>

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:33.050
<i>Other people can't see
Haru-chan and Gintaro,</i>

00:03:33.050 --> 00:03:35.410
<i>so it looks like the 
two of us are alone.</i>

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:37.970
I'm Amamoto. Hi.

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:39.900
I'm Kamio.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:43.200
He goes to a different school, 
but he's Yumi-chan's...

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:43.770
Oh...

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:47.410
Oh.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.570
What was that pause for?

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:51.470
Huh?

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:52.670
It was nothing.

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:56.120
You look like you have 
something you wanna say.

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:57.290
Huh?

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:58.520
Saeki!

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:00.130
Yumi-chan!

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:02.970
Why are you and Kamio here?

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:05.090
Are you on a date?

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:08.400
We're not!

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.810
I'm showing Satoru-kun around town.

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:16.100
Anyway, you should come in 
and see how Mi-chan's doing.

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:17.730
Come in.

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:20.150
<b>Amabuki Temple</b>

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:20.150
A temple, huh...

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:22.440
What's wrong, Gintaro?

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:24.700
Nothing.

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:28.600
Hello.

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:31.330
Well, well.

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:32.850
Glad you could come.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:34.900
Here's a little gift.

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:37.330
Oh, thanks as always.

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:40.080
Sho-chan, is Yumi-chan here?

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:41.910
Yumi-chan!

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:43.760
Hey, there are people 
I don't recognize.

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.760
These are my friends, 
Saeki and Kamio-kun!

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:48.080
Thank you for coming.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:49.580
I'm Shohei's mother.

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:51.270
I'm his older sister, Fujino.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:52.730
I'm Kikuri.

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:54.610
Nice to meet you.

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:55.550
I'm Saeki.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:56.650
Hello.

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:58.610
L-Look, Fuji-nee!

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:00.290
That boy's really cute!

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:01.150
Uh-huh!

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:03.980
When did you become friends 
with this boy, Sho-chan?

00:05:03.980 --> 00:05:05.410
He's so clean!

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:06.740
Uh-huh!

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.030
He's adorable!

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:14.830
Bah, what a pain...

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:16.640
Oh, Serika-oneechan.

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:18.260
Hmm? We have guests?

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:21.840
Serika-san, I finished washing the car.

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:26.300
I need you to come 
shopping with me, then.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:29.440
I have yard work to do.

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:30.760
You can do it later!

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:32.240
No,

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:34.520
it is part of my training.

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:42.280
I love it!

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:44.120
He's so hot!

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:45.860
I'm gonna make him mine!

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:48.960
Sorry...

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:51.160
I wish we had this much fun at home.

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:53.290
It's just me and my dad.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:57.500
I would never want to live here.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:01.870
I think it's time to shave 
that head of yours.

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:03.170
Ugh, old man!

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:06.750
Let's get going.

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:08.380
You wanna see Fug, right?

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:13.140
<i>Shohei-kun must have 
a rough time at home.</i>

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:17.510
Mi-chan.

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:19.860
What are you doing here, Mi-chan?

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:20.980
Come out.

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:22.930
Yumi-chan!

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:24.280
They can see your underwear!

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:27.780
This time, I'm really leaving!

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:30.620
I can't take anymore of this!

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:33.280
I've had enough!

00:06:32.210 --> 00:06:34.200
Come on, not again...

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:36.110
Calm down, Mi-chan.

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:37.250
You okay?

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:41.420
Seriously, what's wrong 
with your place?

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:44.030
Well, actually...

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:45.630
We've been getting visitors...

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:46.130
Huh?

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:48.170
Like this!

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:49.170
What?

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:51.640
I'm going home!

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:51.640
You mean ghosts?

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:54.560
Well, this is a temple, 
so it's not that weird.

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:57.270
You never mentioned 
anything about this!

00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:59.220
It's not that unusual.

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:00.040
Yes, it is.

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:01.210
It's not.

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:02.590
Stop lying!

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:03.180
I'm not!

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:03.730
You are!

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:04.340
I'm not!

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:05.740
Now, now...

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:07.140
Sheesh...

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:10.200
I think it's time to leave.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:11.160
I feel the same way.

00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:17.950
It's not like anyone's 
actually seen a ghost.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:19.420
I've gotten used to it.

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:20.120
So what do you mean?

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:22.580
We've had stuff fall 
down during meditation

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:25.500
and candles going out when 
there wasn't any wind.

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:28.510
The yard gets messed up 
right after we cleaned it.

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:29.880
That's about it.

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:35.860
My old man said that this was 
"part of Buddhist training."

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:39.740
It's possible that Fug can see them.

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:42.720
It's not funny!

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:44.480
Maybe you need to show more 
respect for the dead!

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:45.650
What's that got to do with anything?!

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:47.690
Then why are there ghosts?!

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:47.690
<i>Ghosts...</i>

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:48.550
It's not my fault!

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:53.200
<i>Right, unlike shrines, temples are 
where people are laid to rest.</i>

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:58.880
Gintaro-sama, did you sense that?

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:01.540
Yes, I felt something.

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:07.270
Huh? There's a shrine.

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:08.880
Why? Isn't this a temple?

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:12.010
Oh, it's always been there.

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:14.560
We maintain the place,

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:16.970
but it's not that unusual to 
find a shrine in a temple.

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:20.730
Are you interested, Mako-chan?

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:22.890
You're a true shrine girl.

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:26.890
The gods and Buddhas used 
to be lumped together.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:28.890
It's not that strange.

00:08:29.350 --> 00:08:31.400
Back when the religions 
were mixed together?

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:35.380
What was that?

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:37.080
There it is again.

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:39.330
You can look around if you want.

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:40.310
Huh?

00:08:40.310 --> 00:08:41.270
What do you mean?

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:43.210
What's wrong, Mi-chan?

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:46.330
Wait up, Mi-chan!

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:46.330
Yumi-chan?

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:48.890
Mi-chan, there's nothing 
to be scared about!

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:50.890
Gintaro, does that 
little shrine have...

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:53.510
The size of a shrine doesn't matter.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:56.550
It looks like they're here...

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:02.430
and they like to play pranks.

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:04.390
Heralds!

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:08.790
Satoru, let's go look!

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:12.070
Good grief...

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:15.570
They see heralds every day.

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:18.560
It's starting to happen a lot more.

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:20.570
How did this fall over?

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:41.060
See that, Fuu-chan?

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:42.970
You bet, Fuku-chan!

00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:44.970
This is fun!

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:46.980
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:49.890
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:52.400
Look at the stupid looks on 
those humans' faces, Fuku-chan!

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:54.860
So stupid, Fuu-chan!

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:57.240
But something's not right.

00:09:57.240 --> 00:10:00.070
Humans aren't supposed 
to be able to see us.

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:02.830
And look at that little weirdo.

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:05.330
Oh, there's also a big one.

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:08.500
Hey!

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:10.600
Get down here!

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:12.710
Who're you calling a little weirdo?!

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:15.300
What's going on?

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:16.640
F-Fuu-chan...

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:17.970
Fuku-chan...

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:19.680
Scary!

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:22.440
Hey, Gin. You're scaring them.

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:25.640
I haven't done a thing.

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:26.590
Haru.

00:10:26.590 --> 00:10:29.470
But they were making fun of me!

00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:29.950
Good grief...

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:31.810
Aren't you heralds?

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:34.560
Have you never spoken 
to a human before?

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:38.030
Are you a herald, too, Gramps?

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:40.420
Gramps...

00:10:40.420 --> 00:10:43.050
You look totally different than us.

00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:44.490
I'm a fox.

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:46.400
Oh, a fox!

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:48.790
We're monkeys!

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:50.000
Yep!

00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:52.210
I know, I know...

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:53.940
I know, Fuu-chan!

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:55.630
This is what Grandpa was talking about!

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:57.860
He said there were other 
types of heralds out there!

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:01.770
That's right! This is great!

00:11:01.770 --> 00:11:03.140
It's our first time seeing one!

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:05.800
Yay!

00:11:04.650 --> 00:11:05.800
Everything clear now?

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:08.710
They're responsible for 
that ghost business.

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:11.970
It doesn't look like there are 
any humans around with the Sight.

00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:13.680
Satisfied now?

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:15.050
Let's go home.

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:16.610
Huh? We can't go!

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:19.530
We need to talk to them and
 tell them to stop their pranks.

00:11:20.210 --> 00:11:21.900
We're outsiders.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:24.830
I think it's best if we don't interfere.

00:11:25.390 --> 00:11:26.160
But...

00:11:26.590 --> 00:11:28.580
You can stay behind by yourself, then!

00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:31.500
Human! Human!

00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:36.650
You can see me?

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:38.370
Can you really see me?

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:39.400
Really?

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:40.010
Yup.

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:41.940
Are you leaving now?

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:46.140
So cute!

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:47.390
Yay!

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:48.040
Honestly...

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:49.640
Cute, cute, cute.

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:51.710
Human women have no self-control.

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:55.010
No fair!

00:11:55.010 --> 00:11:56.440
Fuu-chan gets all the fun!

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:02.100
Hey, am I cute? Am I?

00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:02.910
S-Sure.

00:12:03.730 --> 00:12:04.850
Yay!

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:07.770
Hey! Get off of Satoru!

00:12:07.770 --> 00:12:09.370
What's this ribbon?

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:10.800
You don't deserve it!

00:12:18.280 --> 00:12:20.130
My ribbon!

00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:24.760
H-Haru, stay calm.

00:12:25.830 --> 00:12:27.190
I'm mad now!

00:12:27.190 --> 00:12:28.800
Gintaro, catch them!

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:29.970
We need to punish them!

00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:31.590
Too much effort.

00:12:31.590 --> 00:12:33.790
Get to it!

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:34.820
Now, now...

00:12:34.820 --> 00:12:37.650
You're their elder, Haru-chan.

00:12:38.670 --> 00:12:40.150
Funny face!

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:44.440
Hey, can you cut it—

00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:46.120
Fox!

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:47.870
Scary face!

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:51.350
Ow!

00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:56.130
If you're mad, follow us up here!

00:12:56.780 --> 00:12:58.190
In your face!

00:12:58.190 --> 00:12:59.190
Can't do it!

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:01.490
Hey!

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:10.190
Nothing good ever happens 
when I leave the shrine.

00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:11.590
What do we do, Gin?

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:14.050
Hold it right there!

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:18.290
There's no difference between 
human brats and herald brats.

00:13:19.550 --> 00:13:20.900
Okay, Makoto.

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:22.530
Let's get this over with 
so we can go home.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:28.260
You're fast, Gramps!

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:29.590
Amazing!

00:13:29.590 --> 00:13:30.860
Get 'em, Gintaro!

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:32.040
Round 'em up and punish them!

00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:34.710
You're getting punished, too.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:38.380
Now cut it out!

00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:41.550
Gin!

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:44.930
Stupid! Keep your voice down!

00:13:44.930 --> 00:13:45.810
S-Sorry...

00:13:45.810 --> 00:13:48.350
Mi-chan, where are you?

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:50.850
Oh?

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:53.990
What's this?

00:13:53.990 --> 00:13:55.310
Did I interrupt something?

00:13:55.900 --> 00:13:56.730
It's not what you think!

00:13:57.240 --> 00:13:58.310
Sorry!

00:13:58.310 --> 00:13:59.330
Yumi-chan!

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:00.520
Wide open!

00:14:05.090 --> 00:14:06.700
We made her cry!

00:14:11.630 --> 00:14:14.270
What is with today?

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:17.620
Man, I wanna go home...

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:20.390
Sorry, the altar fell over.

00:14:20.390 --> 00:14:22.040
Didn't mean to scare everyone.

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:23.990
Oh, Shohei.

00:14:23.990 --> 00:14:26.230
I can't find Mi-chan.

00:14:26.620 --> 00:14:28.800
Maybe she ran into the graveyard?

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:30.820
Let's look over there.

00:14:32.030 --> 00:14:33.220
Grr!

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:35.430
Gintaro, catch them quick!

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:37.040
I've done enough.

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:39.270
You need to calm down.

00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:42.350
Fuu-chan, let's do it!

00:14:43.620 --> 00:14:44.730
Ta-da!

00:14:51.020 --> 00:14:53.390
What do you think you're doing?!

00:14:53.390 --> 00:14:54.560
Ouch!

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:55.990
It was just the wind!

00:14:57.540 --> 00:14:59.770
Oh, so you can control the wind.

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:02.330
Must come in handy when 
you're playing pranks.

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:04.250
Did they do that?

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:08.350
Hey, it's harder to play pranks 
when humans are watching us.

00:15:08.350 --> 00:15:10.390
They're a real pain.

00:15:10.390 --> 00:15:11.720
Hey!

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:14.180
Heralds aren't supposed to play pranks!

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:16.180
Huh? Why not?

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:18.380
It's so much fun to play pranks!

00:15:18.380 --> 00:15:20.320
Everyone forgets about the sad things!

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:21.900
Everyone's happy!

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:24.660
Hey, are you gonna try to catch us?

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:26.320
That means Gramps is it!

00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:29.280
I don't have time to waste on you!

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:32.170
Hey! Wait up!

00:15:32.170 --> 00:15:33.610
No way!

00:15:38.050 --> 00:15:39.100
Stop running around!

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:40.710
Can you all shut up?!

00:15:41.910 --> 00:15:43.710
I hate brats.

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:46.200
Stop! This isn't fair!

00:15:46.200 --> 00:15:48.880
Let's play tag!

00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:56.560
Haru!

00:15:57.060 --> 00:15:58.770
Try and catch us!

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:04.690
Satoru!

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:06.790
I've had enough! Let's go home!

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:08.400
Are you okay, Haru-chan?

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:15.240
Stupid girl always has to meddle.

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:21.930
No more!

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:24.730
Honestly, it's like you're 
still in grade school.

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:25.080
Say, Satoru-kun...

00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:28.270
Why do you think those 
heralds are playing pranks?

00:16:28.270 --> 00:16:30.720
Because they think it's fun!

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:32.340
There's no other reason!

00:16:33.030 --> 00:16:33.840
But...

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:36.800
Their pranks are causing fights

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:38.870
and scaring people who 
think they're ghosts

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:41.420
when they're really heralds.

00:16:41.970 --> 00:16:44.200
Haru-chan, would you want people 
to think you're a ghost?

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:46.230
No...

00:16:47.030 --> 00:16:49.790
This place is a temple,
 there's no one with the Sight,

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:50.900
and they're still kids...

00:16:51.380 --> 00:16:54.200
Maybe they've been 
isolated from humans.

00:16:54.710 --> 00:16:57.200
Let's go talk to the chief priest.

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:58.800
He may know something.

00:16:59.110 --> 00:16:59.740
Yeah.

00:17:00.860 --> 00:17:04.090
We maintain this shrine currently,

00:17:04.090 --> 00:17:07.000
but it was here when the 
temple was originally built,

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:11.630
and our temple is actually 
using the shrine grounds.

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:13.840
Really?

00:17:14.810 --> 00:17:16.230
I already taught you that!

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:23.500
Long ago, there were many 
monkeys living around here.

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:27.990
That may be why the heralds for 
this shrine are monkey spirits.

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:33.240
When Shinto and Buddhism were 
separated, the temple was larger,

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:37.570
and the shrine was uninhabited, 
so it was left like this.

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:41.360
Well, I suppose that the 
temple grew so large

00:17:41.360 --> 00:17:44.390
because it benefited from 
being near the shrine.

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:46.450
Monkeys are the symbol of victory.

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:49.540
Sacred monkeys are the key to victory.

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:54.330
So we are as grateful to the 
gods as we are to the Buddhas.

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:03.360
I'll go see if Mi-chan 
is in the graveyard.

00:18:03.360 --> 00:18:05.810
We'll look over there, then.

00:18:06.590 --> 00:18:09.900
There used to be lots 
of monkeys around.

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:11.980
Maybe they're lonely.

00:18:12.540 --> 00:18:15.660
They may be trying to 
chase the humans out.

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:19.490
They used to live happily 
with their friends,

00:18:20.230 --> 00:18:23.280
but once the temple was constructed, 
the monkeys had to leave.

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:26.370
I-It didn't look like they were 
trying to chase anyone out.

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:27.970
I wouldn't be so sure.

00:18:27.970 --> 00:18:29.970
Heralds remember their 
past, so this can happen

00:18:29.970 --> 00:18:33.130
when you have young heralds 
without humans who can see them.

00:18:34.370 --> 00:18:36.880
There were humans I truly hated...

00:18:39.790 --> 00:18:41.260
Why don't you ask them?

00:18:43.170 --> 00:18:45.020
Let us go!

00:18:45.230 --> 00:18:46.070
Gin.

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:49.390
We keep running away 
but he still finds us!

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:51.360
Why?! Why?!

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:52.940
That's a secret.

00:19:01.270 --> 00:19:03.820
What? Chase out the humans?

00:19:03.820 --> 00:19:06.570
We don't want to do that!

00:19:06.570 --> 00:19:09.500
Then why are you playing pranks?!

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:14.460
Because the humans who come 
here all look so unhappy.

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:18.760
They're always crying and mourning.

00:19:19.520 --> 00:19:22.390
It's too much for us to bear.

00:19:22.610 --> 00:19:26.970
So we thought we could cheer them 
up by scaring them a little.

00:19:27.320 --> 00:19:28.530
Was it fun?

00:19:28.530 --> 00:19:29.060
No!

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:31.490
Plus, that's what Grandpa said.

00:19:31.490 --> 00:19:32.920
Grandpa?

00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:34.860
The herald who used to be here.

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:37.320
But he's gone now...

00:19:37.520 --> 00:19:39.370
Fuu, Fuku.

00:19:39.370 --> 00:19:43.320
You don't need to be sad if the 
other monkeys stop coming.

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:45.440
They've merely been replaced by humans.

00:19:46.560 --> 00:19:49.580
Many things will happen 
as more humans come,

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:52.210
but all you have to do is smile.

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:55.250
After all, we monkeys bring victory.

00:19:55.440 --> 00:20:00.670
If you don't smile, nobody will win.

00:20:00.910 --> 00:20:04.270
That's why we want to have fun!

00:20:04.270 --> 00:20:07.390
Plus, there's a temple 
and graveyard around.

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:10.620
We're going to live a long time,

00:20:10.620 --> 00:20:13.860
so we have to watch over 
this place for the humans,

00:20:13.860 --> 00:20:17.400
the other monkeys, and Grandpa.

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:20.360
That's our job.

00:20:21.480 --> 00:20:23.780
Well, I guess we might have 
taken the pranks too far.

00:20:24.210 --> 00:20:25.710
We're sorry.

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:30.680
But you were trying to 
cheer everyone up, right?

00:20:30.680 --> 00:20:31.510
Yeah!

00:20:32.310 --> 00:20:36.800
Humans know how to pick 
themselves back up.

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:41.220
Yep, so you don't need 
to play pranks anymore.

00:20:43.160 --> 00:20:46.320
What? That's no fun!

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:49.470
We enjoy scaring humans!

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:51.860
It's the most fun we've ever had!

00:20:51.860 --> 00:20:53.240
We can't stop!

00:20:54.590 --> 00:20:56.610
H-Hey!

00:20:57.830 --> 00:21:00.010
What? Monkey heralds?

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:03.420
You're a big fan of the occult, huh?

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:08.420
But I like the idea that the 
gods were playing pranks.

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:11.290
It bodes well for our temple.

00:21:11.800 --> 00:21:15.250
I don't see anything wrong with having 
a monkey spirit or two around.

00:21:16.050 --> 00:21:18.170
We already have plenty 
of monkeys around.

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:20.170
Is she talking about us?

00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:22.510
We should be grateful that the gods

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:25.600
have joined the Buddha 
in blessing this temple.

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:32.520
Bye-bye!

00:21:37.660 --> 00:21:39.810
I'm worried about them.

00:21:40.370 --> 00:21:43.060
We should probably check on 
them every once in a while.

00:21:43.660 --> 00:21:45.520
It'll be fine.

00:21:45.940 --> 00:21:48.200
They didn't mean any harm.

00:21:48.670 --> 00:21:51.330
Shohei-kun's family 
didn't seem to mind.

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:52.600
That's good.

00:21:53.510 --> 00:21:54.590
You're a fool.

00:21:55.370 --> 00:21:57.710
They don't believe that heralds exist.

00:21:59.390 --> 00:22:01.290
That's not important.

00:22:01.580 --> 00:22:05.840
It's our job to serve as a bridge 
between heralds and humans.

00:22:06.990 --> 00:22:08.480
Still, I thought it was interesting.

00:22:08.880 --> 00:22:10.420
Fuu-chan and Fuku-chan

00:22:10.420 --> 00:22:13.310
didn't seem to differentiate  
between the temple and shrine.

00:22:14.340 --> 00:22:16.390
The Japanese gods are wonderful.

00:22:17.040 --> 00:22:21.640
Yeah, the Japanese gods are about 
as irresponsible as you get.

00:22:21.640 --> 00:22:24.070
You should say that 
they're broad-minded!

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:19.850
<b>Preview</b>

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:19.850
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:24:10.780 --> 00:24:12.940
Heralds serve as 
messengers of the gods.

00:24:12.940 --> 00:24:17.350
There are foxes, monkeys, 
rabbits, turtles, crows,

00:24:17.350 --> 00:24:19.650
and other types of heralds.

00:24:19.970 --> 00:24:30.000
<b>Humans are Strange</b>

00:24:20.040 --> 00:24:22.520
Next time: "Humans are Strange."

00:24:22.840 --> 00:24:24.930
May fortune be with you.
